§ `Schedule 12 -- Arrangements in which registered third country auditors are required to participate`

-- src:20657 | 1 (1) The arrangements referred to in section 1242(1)(a) are appropriate arrangements—
-- src:20658 | (a) for enabling the performance by the registered third country auditor of functions related to the audit of UK-traded third country companies to be monitored by means of inspections carried out under the arrangements, and
-- src:20659 | (b) for ensuring that the carrying out of such monitoring and inspections is done independently of the registered third country auditor.
@ref sch 12 para 1(1) Arrangements for independent monitoring of audits of UK-traded third country companies (src:20657-20659)
GIVEN `the arrangements are appropriate for enabling the performance by the registered third country auditor of functions related to the audit of UK-traded third country companies to be monitored by means of inspections carried out under the arrangements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the arrangements are appropriate for ensuring that the carrying out of such monitoring and inspections is done independently of the registered third country auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 12 para 1(1) the arrangements are appropriate arrangements` MEANS
    IF `the arrangements are appropriate for enabling the performance by the registered third country auditor of functions related to the audit of UK-traded third country companies to be monitored by means of inspections carried out under the arrangements`
       AND `the arrangements are appropriate for ensuring that the carrying out of such monitoring and inspections is done independently of the registered third country auditor`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The arrangements referred to in section 1242(1)(a) are appropriate arrangements—"

-- src:20662 | 2 (1) The arrangements referred to in section 1242(1)(b) are appropriate arrangements—
-- src:20663 | (a) for the carrying out of investigations into matters arising in connection with the performance of functions related to the audit of UK-traded third country companies by the registered third country auditor,
-- src:20664 | (b) where it appears to be desirable following the conclusion of such investigations—
-- src:20665 | (i) for the holding, subject to sub-paragraph (1A), of disciplinary hearings relating to the registered third country auditor,
-- src:20666 | (ii) unless the interests of justice otherwise require, for any such hearings to be held in public, and
-- src:20667 | (iii) for decisions to be made as to whether (and, if so, what) disciplinary action should be taken against the registered third country auditor, and
-- src:20668 | (c) for ensuring that the carrying out of those investigations, the holding of those hearings and the making of those decisions are done independently of the registered third country auditor.
@ref sch 12 para 2(1) Arrangements for independent investigations for disciplinary purposes (src:20662-20668)
GIVEN `the arrangements are appropriate for the carrying out of investigations into matters arising in connection with the performance of functions related to the audit of UK-traded third country companies by the registered third country auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to be desirable, following the conclusion of such investigations, to hold disciplinary hearings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the arrangements provide for the holding of disciplinary hearings relating to the registered third country auditor, subject to sub-paragraph (1A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the arrangements provide for any such hearings to be held in public unless the interests of justice otherwise require` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the arrangements provide for decisions to be made as to whether and if so what disciplinary action should be taken against the registered third country auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the arrangements are appropriate for ensuring that the carrying out of those investigations, the holding of those hearings and the making of those decisions are done independently of the registered third country auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 12 para 2(1) the arrangements are appropriate arrangements` MEANS
    IF    `the arrangements are appropriate for the carrying out of investigations into matters arising in connection with the performance of functions related to the audit of UK-traded third country companies by the registered third country auditor`
       AND (    (NOT `it appears to be desirable, following the conclusion of such investigations, to hold disciplinary hearings`)
             OR (    `the arrangements provide for the holding of disciplinary hearings relating to the registered third country auditor, subject to sub-paragraph (1A)`
                 AND `the arrangements provide for any such hearings to be held in public unless the interests of justice otherwise require`
                 AND `the arrangements provide for decisions to be made as to whether and if so what disciplinary action should be taken against the registered third country auditor`))
       AND `the arrangements are appropriate for ensuring that the carrying out of those investigations, the holding of those hearings and the making of those decisions are done independently of the registered third country auditor`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The arrangements referred to in section 1242(1)(b) are appropriate arrangements"

