-- src:20682 | 4 (1) The registered third country auditor must pay any of the costs of maintaining any relevant arrangements which the arrangements provide are to be paid by it.
-- src:20683 | (2) For this purpose “relevant arrangements” are arrangements within paragraph 1 or 2 in which the registered third country auditor is obliged to participate.
@ref sch 12 para 4 The registered third country auditor must pay the costs the arrangements provide it is to pay (src:20682-20683)
GIVEN `the arrangements are within paragraph 1 or 2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the registered third country auditor is obliged to participate in the arrangements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the arrangements provide that the costs are to be paid by the registered third country auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the registered third country auditor has paid those costs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 12 para 4 the registered third country auditor has paid the costs it must pay` MEANS
    IF    `the arrangements are within paragraph 1 or 2`
       AND `the registered third country auditor is obliged to participate in the arrangements`
       AND `the arrangements provide that the costs are to be paid by the registered third country auditor`
    THEN IF `the registered third country auditor has paid those costs`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The registered third country auditor must pay any of the costs of maintaining any relevant arrangements which the arrangements provide are to be paid by it"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any relevant arrangements which the arrangements provide are to be paid by it"

